Overlay patch 0028: THE sibling-wide fuzzy-audio fix — SYNC WAVE 2 addendum B
(2ship 0024, device-confirmed 2026-07-19). Starship's GameEngine::HandleAudioThread
is the OLD coupled loop: a plain cv_to_thread.wait() that produces audio ONLY
on the game loop's per-tick notify. On iOS the game loop IS the UIKit main
thread, so touch-event/redraw bursts (a pressed thumb delivers up to 120 Hz)
delay the notify past the ring's headroom -> the SDL backend drains -> crackle
("fuzzy audio", every sibling except SoH, whose upstream already evolved this
loop). Starship's report is always-on fuzz (STARSHIP QUARANTINE) — the audio
path, not the input path.
Fix: port SoH's loop shape — QoS user-interactive on the audio thread + 5 ms
self-pump (wait_for) + producer guard + pre-buffer reservoir — preserving
Starship's processing/cv_from_thread handshake and its DYNAMIC channel count
(GetNumAudioChannels, not a fixed 2). CRITICAL degeneracy check (addendum B):
Starship inits DesiredBuffered=1680 (context->Init {32000,1024,1680,...}) —
same regime as 2S2H, where SoH's `Buffered + burst <= Desired` formula
allowed production only under ~96 samples (WORSE than unfixed). Gate on the
documented intent instead: produce while `Buffered <= Desired` (skip-when-
above; overshoot bounded to one burst). Tracks min/max buffered into atomics
the 0017 rev4 probe reports as aud_min/aud_max (0 = underrun; the retest
instrument). __IOS__-gated: the macOS build keeps the pristine loop.

